F-QS5: refuse Wi-Fi credentials

Quick Share can share a Wi-Fi network: the introduction carries
WifiCredentialsMetadata (the SSID and security type) and, once accepted,
a BYTES payload with the password. Upstream offers it to the user like
a text and then parses the password out of the payload; on any parse
error it logs the error, whose message includes the whole payload
buffer, password and all, at error level.

Sukkula refuses these outright (spec F-QS5): a network credential is
only useful to join the network, which Sukkula never does (S8), and a
peer that pushes one is asking the user to change network on its
say-so. An introduction that carries any Wi-Fi credentials is answered
UNSUPPORTED_ATTACHMENT_TYPE before the user is asked, whatever else it
offers, and the connection ends. The credential payload parser, the
Wifi variants of TextPayloadInfo, TextPayloadType, TransferPayload and
TransferPayloadKind, and the SecurityType plumbing go.

Findings: F-QS5, S8, S9. Report: docs/UPSTREAM-QUICKSHARE.md R5.
